---
// A privacy policy that is short because the site genuinely does very
// little. No advertising pixels, no social embeds, no third-party fonts.
// That is a design decision with a privacy policy as its receipt - and a
// policy that can be read in two minutes and is actually true is worth more
// than four pages of boilerplate describing trackers this shop does not run.
//
// 31 OCT: THIS PAGE USED TO SAY "NO ANALYTICS" AND THAT STOPPED BEING TRUE.
// The shop now counts its own page views, because there was no other way to
// know whether anyone was visiting. The moment that shipped, this page had
// to change - a policy that describes a shop which no longer exists is the
// same misrepresentation as a price that does not match the feed, and it is
// the one kind nobody notices because nobody rereads their own policy. The
// section below says exactly what is counted and what is not stored. If the
// counting ever changes, this page changes in the same commit.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { B } from '../lib/shop';
import { edge, TTL_STATIC } from '../lib/cache';
const addr = (B.registered_address ?? []).join(', ');
edge(Astro.response, TTL_STATIC);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description={`How ${B.legal_name} handles your data. No advertising trackers, no third-party analytics, no third-party fonts. One cookie-free basket stored in your own browser.`}
>
  <div class="wrap page narrow">
    <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>

    <p class="prose">
      {B.legal_name} is the data controller for this website. We can be
      reached at <a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a> or by post at
      {' '}{addr}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect, and only when you order</h2>
    <table class="plain">
      <tr><th>Name and delivery address</th><td>To make and post your order. Kept for 6 years, because HMRC requires us to keep records of sales.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Email address</th><td>To send your order confirmation and tell you when it is posted.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Order details</th><td>So we can honour the returns policy and answer questions about what you bought.</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="prose">
      The lawful basis is performance of a contract — we cannot send you a
      print without knowing where to send it — and, for the records we are
      required to keep, legal obligation.
    </p>

    <h2>How we count visits</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      We keep a simple count of how many pages are viewed, so we can tell
      whether anyone is finding the shop. It runs on our own server — no
      Google Analytics, no third party, and nothing is shared with anyone.
    </p>
    <table class="plain">
      <tr><th>What is recorded</th><td>The page viewed, the time, the website that linked you here if any, and the country your connection is in.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>What is not recorded</th><td><strong>Your IP address is never stored.</strong> It is turned into a short scrambled code, together with your browser type and a secret that changes every midnight, so that two visits on the same day can be told apart — and nothing more. The code cannot be turned back into you, and tomorrow's code for the same person is different.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>How long</th><td>90 days, then deleted automatically.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Lawful basis</th><td>Legitimate interest — knowing whether a shop is being visited. No cookie is set for this, so you have not been asked to accept one.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>No Google Analytics, and no analytics company of any kind. The
        counting above is ours, on our own server.</li>
      <li>No advertising or remarketing pixels. Nothing follows you around.</li>
      <li>No third-party fonts, icon services or social embeds — this page
        loads from one server, ours.</li>
      <li>No marketing emails unless you explicitly ask for them. There is
        no mailing list.</li>
      <li>We never sell or rent your data. To anyone, for any price.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      This site sets <strong>no tracking cookies</strong>, which is why you
      have not been asked to accept any — not for the visit counting above,
      which works without one, and not for anything else. Your basket is
      stored in your own browser using local storage and never reaches us
      until you check out. (One cookie exists on this domain: the one that
      keeps the shop's owner signed in to their own private admin page. It
      is never set for a customer.)
      Stripe sets its own cookies on its payment page to prevent fraud; that
      happens on Stripe's page, under
      {' '}<a href="https://stripe.com/gb/privacy" rel="noopener nofollow">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else sees your data</h2>
    <table class="plain">
      <tr><th>Stripe Payments UK Ltd</th><td>Takes the payment. They receive your name, email and card details; we never see the card number.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Our delivery courier</th><td>Receives your name and address to deliver the parcel.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Cloudflare</th><td>Hosts this website and serves the images. Processes your IP address to deliver the page and block attacks.</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="prose">That is the complete list.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      You can ask us for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask
      us to delete it — except for the sales records HMRC requires us to
      keep. Email <a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a> and we will
      respond within one month. If you are unhappy with how we have handled
      it you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
      {' '}<a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener nofollow">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
